messages.body_plain:
Dear S-Plus users,

I am porting functions that are working well with SP2000 to
S-PLUS 6.0 Rel. 2 (Windows 2000). Some of these functions
use the .Call interface to replace the .C interface with the
pointers argument. These functions are compiled 
with Visual C++ 6.0 through the CHAPTER -m command.

Testing has revealed some problems. All functions work apparently well 
after  being loaded the first time. But if I detach the library and 
reattach it  afterwards and try to use them again, then some of them 
do not work anymore.

Let me explain with a simplified example:

>libary("mscdll5",lib.loc=...,first=T) #load library for the first time
>.Call("fnMscFile",as.character("aa001.msc"))

This works fine. The C-function (see source code below) creates and 
returns a list with two elements. 

>detach(2)                            
>libary("msdll5",lib.loc=...,first=T) 
.Call("fnMscFile",as.character("aa001.msc"))

This time, nothing is returned and there is no error message (Note
that with the simplified function below, it takes detaching and reattaching
the libary several times before the problem occurs). It is as if the 
C function is not anymore called.

Can somebody give me an idea of what could be wrong? 

Gabriel Baud-Bovy

-----------------------------------------
#include  <S.h>

s_object *fnMscFile(s_object *SFname) {
        S_EVALUATOR

        s_object *SList;
        s_object *SPos;
        s_object *SLabels;

        *SPos = NEW_INTEGER(10);
        *SLabels = NEW_CHARACTER(10);
        *SList = NEW_LIST(2);

        SET_ELEMENT(SList,0,SLabels);
        SET_ELEMENT(SList,1,SPos);
        return(SList);
}
